From 44dce9245f1b49b3f7079aa86df558a54bf27759 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 16:03:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] freedreno/a2xx: enable HW fast-clear on A22X to fix GMEM
 background clear

On A220 the non-fast clear-quad path does not clear the GMEM tiles: a
glClear leaves the background unwritten (reads back as 0,0,0,0 -
transparent / "white", instead of the glClearColor). Confirmed with a probe
that wrote a hardcoded colour to the clear shader's CONST[0] and never saw
it reach the framebuffer in GMEM mode (it works in sysmem). The HW
fast-clear (CLEAR_COLOR + RB_COPY_CONTROL) is the only path that actually
clears GMEM, but fd2_clear_fast() early-returned for anything not a20x
("TODO: need to test performance on a22x").

Enable it for a2xx, and extend the 32K GMEM page alignment the fast-clear
requires from a20x to a2xx in gmem_key_init() (freedreno_gmem.c). The
background now clears to the correct colour (gl-capture: 26,51,76,255 for
glClearColor(0.1,0.2,0.3,1.0)), deterministically, with no GPU lockup -
the CP_LOAD_CONSTANT_CONTEXT this path uses is stable in this usage.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_draw.c  | 11 +++++++++--
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c |  3 ++-
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_draw.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_draw.c
index cc152eb9b11..d3b4b336b06 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_draw.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_draw.c
@@ -445,8 +445,15 @@ fd2_clear_fast(struct fd_context *ctx, unsigned buffers,
    int depth_size = -1; /* -1: no clear, 0: clear 16-bit, 1: clear 32-bit */
    int color_size = -1;
 
-   /* TODO: need to test performance on a22x */
-   if (!is_a20x(ctx->screen))
+   /*
+    * Enable the HW fast-clear for A22X too. The non-fast clear-quad path does
+    * NOT clear the GMEM tiles on A220 (the background comes out unwritten,
+    * 0,0,0,0 = transparent/"white"), so the fast clear (which clears GMEM via
+    * CLEAR_COLOR + RB_COPY_CONTROL) is the only working GMEM clear. Note this
+    * path uses CP_LOAD_CONSTANT_CONTEXT (below) which has been a hang hazard
+    * on a2xx - watch for GPU lockups.
+    */
+   if (!is_a2xx(ctx->screen))
       return false;
 
    if (buffers & PIPE_CLEAR_COLOR)
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
index 9f7124dfdee..bba981a4ca8 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
@@ -525,9 +525,10 @@ gmem_key_init(struct fd_batch *batch, bool assume_zs, bool no_scis_opt)
       key->height = scissor->maxy + 1 - key->miny;
    }
 
-   if (is_a20x(screen) && batch->cleared) {
+   if (is_a2xx(screen) && batch->cleared) {
       /* under normal circumstances the requirement would be 4K
        * but the fast clear path requires an alignment of 32K
+       * (a22x uses the fast clear too - see fd2_clear_fast)
        */
       key->gmem_page_align = 8;
    } else if (is_a6xx(screen)) {
-- 
